# Enemy grav-tether: an NPC that pins you instead of just shooting at you.
#
# Lives in the TETHER addon, not ai/. A brain is only a label - brain_add resolves it
# against the story's label table - so nothing makes it belong with the generic AI, and
# putting it there forced `requires grav_tether` onto an addon every mission uses. The
# addon that owns the mechanic owns the behavior that uses it.
#
# Deliberately routed through the ordinary tow, so every rule a player lives under
# applies here too - it cannot grab a ship above the speed limit, mass decides who
# actually gets dragged, and a hard hit shakes the beam loose. An enemy ability that
# ignored the constraints layer would be the win button the layer exists to prevent.

=== ai_tether_pin
" Pinning a target with a grav-tether
metadata: ``` yaml
type: brain/npc
pin_range: 2500
pin_rope: 600
```
    yield fail if BRAIN_AGENT.data_set.get("surrender_flag", 0) == 1
    # Already holding someone: keep the beam, do not go shopping for a second victim.
    yield success if grav_tether_involves(BRAIN_AGENT_ID)

    _pin = closest(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, side_hostile_ships(BRAIN_AGENT_ID) & role("__player__"), pin_range * 2)
    yield fail if _pin is None
    yield fail if _pin.distance > pin_range
    yield fail if lm_tether_enemy_grab(BRAIN_AGENT_ID, _pin.id, pin_rope) is None
    yield success


# The counter-play, ticked for every pinned player: burn hard away and you tear loose.
# BOTH the burn and the clock are required, so breaking free is something the crew DOES.
=== lm_tether_break_watch
--- ltbw_loop
    await delay_sim(1)
    for _pinned in to_object_list(role("__player__")):
        if grav_tether_involves(_pinned.id):
            lm_tether_break_free(_pinned.id)
    jump ltbw_loop
